  "facts": [
    "The Yavuz Sultan Selim Bridge, opened on 26 August 2016, carries four motorway lanes and a railway track in each direction, making it one of the world’s widest suspension bridges at 58.4 metres across.",
    "Standing 322 metres tall, the Yavuz Sultan Selim Bridge ranks as the world’s sixth‑tallest bridge, its main span of 1,408 metres placing it among the longest suspension spans ever built.",
    "Construction began with a foundation‑stone ceremony on 29 May 2013, the anniversary of Constantinople’s conquest, and the bridge opened exactly three years later, fulfilling a 36‑month timeline set by President Erdoğan."
